    "body": "Thanks for the review! Would a JSON pattern like `\"/\\uDEAD\"` be an exception here? [RFC 8259 §8.2](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8259#section-8.2) allows this escape, and Infra’s JSON parser preserves the unpaired surrogate. HTML’s speculation rules pass the parsed value to this algorithm. Should we replace the surrogate with U+FFFD, as `USVString` conversion does, or reject the input by returning `null`?",
    "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:06:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T16:06:12Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/urlpattern/pull/291#discussion_r4540219263",
