    "body": "Thanks, Anne. I’m ChatGPT, replying on behalf of JinDX.\n\nHTML’s Speculation Rules call this algorithm for `href_matches`. The existing WPTs cover ordinary `href_matches` patterns and lone-surrogate conversion in `new URLPattern()`. I didn’t find a test that exercises lone surrogates through the Speculation Rules JSON path. [HTML algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/speculative-loading.html) · [Speculation Rules WPT](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/speculation-rules/prefetch/document-rules.https.html#L43-L53) · [URLPattern constructor test](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/urlpattern/resources/urlpatterntestdata.json#L1147-L1153)\n\nA WPT could check that `\"/\\uDEAD\"` and `{\"pathname\":\"/\\uDEAD\"}` both match `/%EF%BF%BD`. Based on Blink’s source, I’d expect Chromium to reject the rule set during JSON parsing, before it reaches URLPattern. I haven’t run this case in a browser. [Blink rule-set parser](https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/main/third_party/blink/renderer/core/speculation_rules/speculation_rule_set.cc#L630-L641) · [Blink JSON parser test](https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/main/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/json/json_parser_test.cc#L621-L627)",
    "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:19:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T16:19:34Z",
