    "body": "That's interesting, but it seems that JSON parser disagrees with `JSON.parse()` which does allow it. And `JSON.parse()` is what the web platform builds on which also means this PR is correct. But test coverage is important for changes like these.\r\n\r\nI guess that means we can create another test where we have a bogus rule that will cause Chrome to reject the entire JSON response incorrectly.\r\n\r\nIf you're willing you could put ChatGPT to work on a https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt PR.",
