    "body": "+1 to converting to a scalar value string here to match the `USVString` behavior. From Chromium's side, in addition to `blink::ParseJSON` rejecting lone surrogates during `<script type=\"speculationrules\">` parsing, our implementation of *build a URL pattern from an Infra value* ([`ParseURLPatternFromJSON`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/url_pattern/url_pattern_utils.cc;l=17-81)) also constructs `V8URLPatternInput` and `URLPatternInit` directly in C++ from `JSONValue`, bypassing the Web IDL `USVString` binding (`ReplaceUnmatchedSurrogates`). So we'll need to update both the JSON parser and `ParseURLPatternFromJSON` on our side.",
    "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:05:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T17:05:49Z",
